{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward bias in true outcomes vs model: model systematically underpredicts during rising regimes (often by ~2–5 EUR, occasionally more) across most of the 30-day horizon.",
    "Trend/lag error: model behaves like a smoothed/mean-reverting process and reacts too slowly to regime shifts; when the last-30d history turns up, add a positive drift to the whole path rather than only near-term.",
    "Horizon-dependent underprediction: the gap generally widens from ~day 5 onward (mid-to-late horizon misses the sustained rally). Apply an increasing uplift with horizon (e.g., small uplift days 1–3, larger uplift days 10–30).",
    "Post-breakout persistence miss: after prices break above ~66–67, true outcomes tend to stay elevated (high-60s) while the model reverts back to mid-60s. Enforce a higher floor/level shift once a breakout threshold is crossed.",
    "Avoid premature mean reversion after spikes: model often fades strength too quickly; if recent momentum is positive (e.g., last 5–10d slope > 0), dampen any forecasted pullback and shift the path upward.",
    "Volatility/peak underestimation: model misses the amplitude of peaks (true highs ~69–70 while model tops ~66–68). Inflate upside tails during uptrends (e.g., add extra uplift to local maxima / upper quantiles)."
  ]
}
